    lspu:alternateQuestion "Where do I activate my portal account?" ;
    lspu:additionalInfo "Go to this office for: activation of the student portal account." .

lspuadm:Office_BusinessAffairsOffice
    lspu:alternateQuestion "Where do I buy the uniform and shirts?" ,
        "How much are the uniform, shirts and ID lace, and where do I buy them?" ,
        "Where can I buy the uniform and shirts?" ,
        "How much should a new student budget for uniform items?" ,
        "How much money do freshmen need for uniforms?" ,
        "What do I need to buy as a first-year student?" ,
        "How much are all the school items in the first year?" ,
        "What are the extra costs in college?" ;
    lspu:additionalInfo "All of these are bought at the Business Affairs Office (BAO). Uniform fabric: about Php 600-800 (fabric only, so you need a tailor to make the polo and pants, which costs extra). University shirt: Php 400. NSTP shirt: Php 350. PE T-shirt and shorts: Php 500. ID lace: Php 130. The official ID card itself is free for first-year students. If you buy one of each item sold at the BAO, the total is roughly Php 1,980 to 2,180: uniform fabric Php 600-800, University shirt Php 400, NSTP shirt Php 350, PE T-shirt and shorts Php 500, ID lace Php 130. Not included: tailoring for the uniform, books, OJT, transport and housing. Laboratory costs are not an extra: they are already covered by the free tuition. The ID card is free for first-year students." ,
        "Go to this office for: Student ID, and the sale of the ID lace, uniform fabric, University shirt, NSTP shirt and PE uniform." ;
    lspu:audience "New students" ;
    lspu:verificationNote "Prices reported in September 2026 and may change. Confirm whether the Php 500 PE price is per set." ;
    lspu:sourceArticle "Campus information supplied by the ontology maintainer (an LSPU-LB student), September 2026; not from the Handbook or Citizen's Charter" ,
        "Estimate computed by the ontology builder from the maintainer-supplied prices (2026-09); assumes one of each item" .

