lspu:Org_SupremeStudentCouncil
    lspu:alternateQuestion "What is the Supreme Student Council?" ,
        "How many student councils are there?" ,
        "What is the difference between the SSC and a college student council?" ,
        "Who governs the college student councils?" ;
    lspu:additionalInfo "Yes. All 8 colleges (CAS, CBAA, CCS, CCJE, CF, CFND, CIHT and CTE) have their own student council, and there is one Supreme Student Council that governs them at the campus level. The SSC represents students campus-wide and helps organize campus-wide activities, programs and student initiatives." ;
    lspu:audience "New students" ;
    lspu:organizationOfCampus lspu:Campus_LSPULB .

