lspuprog:CTE
    lspu:alternateQuestion "Which college should I choose for teaching?" ;
    lspu:definition "The College of Teacher Education (CTE) offers 9 programs: BS Education majors in English, Filipino, Mathematics, Sciences, and Social Studies; Bachelor of Elementary Education; Bachelor of Technology and Livelihood Education major in Home Economics; Bachelor of Technical-Vocational Teacher Education major in Food and Service Management; and Bachelor of Physical Education. CTE requires no grade lower than 85 in English, Mathematics, and Science for admission." ;
    lspu:programCount "9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> ;
    lspu:collegeOfCampus lspu:Campus_LSPULB .

lspu:AdmReq_ExamAndInterview
    lspu:alternateQuestion "What if my GWA is below the cutoff for my chosen course?" ,
        "My grade is lower than the minimum GWA, can I still apply?" ,
        "Is the GWA cutoff strict?" ,
        "Are there exceptions to the GWA requirement?" ,
        "What can I do if I do not meet the cutoff?" ,
        "Which courses accept a lower GWA?" ,
        "I have a GWA of 86, what can I take?" ,
        "What grade do I need to qualify for admission?" ,
        "What is the minimum GWA for LSPU-LB?" ,
        "What is the GWA requirement for BSIT / Education / Accountancy?" ,
        "Can I apply with a grade of 85?" ,
        "What is the minimum grade to get into LSPU?" ,
        "What GWA is needed for BSIT?" ,
        "What if my GWA is below the cutoff?" ;
    lspu:additionalInfo "Minimum GWA cutoffs range from 85 to 90 depending on the program (LSPU Admission Guidelines, 1st Sem AY 2026-2027, Annex A). GWA 90: BS Accountancy, BS Computer Science, BS Food Technology, BS Nutrition and Dietetics, Bachelor of Physical Education, all five BS Education majors, and Bachelor of Elementary Education (11 programs). GWA 88: BS Psychology, both BS Business Administration majors, BS Tourism Management (4). GWA 87: BS Fisheries, BTLE, BTVTE (3). GWA 85: the three BS Information Technology majors, BS Criminology, BS Hospitality Management (5). Extra conditions: CTE programs require no grade lower than 85 in English, Mathematics, and Science; CCS gives priority to STEM and ICT/ICTS strand applicants." ,
        "The GWA cutoff is strict." ,
        "If your GWA is below the minimum for the program you want, you cannot be admitted to it; your only option is to choose another program with a lower cutoff." ,
        "Cutoffs for 1st Sem AY 2026-2027: GWA 85 for BS Information Technology (3 majors), BS Criminology and BS Hospitality Management; GWA 87 for BS Fisheries, BTLE and BTVTE; GWA 88 for BS Psychology, both BS Business Administration majors and BS Tourism Management; GWA 90 for Accountancy, Computer Science, Food Technology, Nutrition and Dietetics, Physical Education, all five BS Education majors and Elementary Education." ,
        "Example: a GWA of 86 qualifies only for the GWA-85 programs." ,
        "CTE programs also need no grade below 85 in English, Math and Science, and CCS gives priority to STEM and ICT applicants." ,
        "Meeting the cutoff is not enough by itself: applicants must still pass the entrance exam and interview." ,
        "CTE programs also require no grade below 85 in English, Math and Science." ;
    lspu:audience "Applicants, incoming freshmen" ;
    lspu:verificationNote "Cutoffs are for 1st Semester AY 2026-2027 and may change each year." ;
    lspu:sourceArticle "Strictness and lower-cutoff advice: Campus information supplied by the ontology maintainer (an LSPU-LB student), September 2026; not from the Handbook or Citizen's Charter. Cutoff values: LSPU Admission Guidelines, 1st Sem AY 2026-2027, Annex A. Exam and interview: LSPU official website admission pages, text supplied by the ontology maintainer, September 2026; not from the Handbook or Citizen's Charter" ,
        "LSPU Admission Guidelines, 1st Sem AY 2026-2027, Annex A" ;
    lspuprog:sourceDocument "LSPU Admission Guidelines for the 1st Semester of AY 2026-2027, Annex A." .

